import ../../../testing/driver.dl
import lib/text_scan.dl

document view test:
    view group "Current view" using no UI appearance:
        region "First view" using no UI appearance:
            editor "First source" containing "First text" using no UI appearance
        region "Second view" using no UI appearance:
            editor "Second source" containing "Second text" using no UI appearance

set instance to an instance of view test
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 300 by 200 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set group to the control labeled "Current view" in (the address of instance)
require condition (view's control count = 1) reporting "An inactive view participated in keyboard focus"
require condition ((the active UI editor within group in (the address of instance))'s text = "First source") reporting "The view group did not resolve its first editor"
set the text of "First source" in (the address of instance) to "Retained first edit"
set the value of "Current view" in (the address of instance) to 1
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set drawn to (view's window as a pointer to test UI surface)'s drawn
require condition (drawn contains "Second text") reporting "The selected view was not painted"
require condition ((drawn contains "Retained first edit") = false) reporting "An inactive view was painted"
require condition ((the active UI editor within group in (the address of instance))'s text = "Second source") reporting "The active editor did not follow the selected view"
set the value of "Current view" in (the address of instance) to 0
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (((view's window as a pointer to test UI surface)'s drawn) contains "Retained first edit") reporting "Changing views discarded editor data"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "View groups retain panels while selecting their layout, painting and focus."
